%N A358088 Number of pairs (s,t) with s and t squarefree, 1 <= s < t <= n and s | t.
%H A358088 Robert Israel, <a href="/A358088/b358088.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%F A358088 a(n) = Sum_{i=1..n} Sum_{k=1..i-1} mu(i)^2 * mu(k)^2 * c(i/k), where c(n) = 1 - ceiling(n) + floor(n).
%F A358088 a(n) - a(n-1) = 2^A001222(n) - 1 if n is squarefree, otherwise 0. - _Robert Israel_, Sep 18 2026
%e A358088 a(9) = 7. The pairs are (1,2), (1,3), (1,5), (1,6), (1,7), (2,6) and (3,6).
%p A358088 g:= proc(t) local F,m;
%p A358088   F:= ifactors(t)[2];
%p A358088   if max(F[..,2])=1 then 2^nops(F)-1 else 0 fi
%p A358088 end proc:
%p A358088 ListTools:-PartialSums(map(g, [$1..100])); # _Robert Israel_, Sep 18 2026
